An activity a plugin declares cannot say it supports picture-in-picture: the
compiler writes a fixed set of attributes and `supportsPictureInPicture` is
not among them, so a player declared by a plugin would be refused the window
by the platform however it asked. The attribute is written where the
declaration names it, and nowhere else.

--- a/vendor/nativephp/mobile/src/Plugins/Compilers/AndroidPluginCompiler.php
+++ b/vendor/nativephp/mobile/src/Plugins/Compilers/AndroidPluginCompiler.php
@@ -1151,3 +1151,6 @@
         if (isset($activity['configChanges'])) {
             $attrs[] = "android:configChanges=\"{$activity['configChanges']}\"";
         }
+        if (isset($activity['supportsPictureInPicture'])) {
+            $attrs[] = 'android:supportsPictureInPicture="'.($activity['supportsPictureInPicture'] ? 'true' : 'false').'"';
+        }
